    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/bliv-en-del-af-fremtidens-forskning-som-phd-paa-aarhus-bss-psykologi": {
      "title": "Join the future of research as a PhD student",
      "description": "Join the future of research as a PhD student at Aarhus BSS, Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences Join the future of research as a PhD student at Aarhus BSS, Psychology and Behavioural Sciences Deadline 7 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Feb Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences Bartholins Allé 11 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Feb 2027 - 31 Jan 2030 ID: 165662 Apply Aarhus BSS is now inviting applications for a number of PhD scholarships across our six academic PhD programmes. This call concerns the PhD programme in Psychology and Behavioural Sciences. We are looking for candidates who are highly motivated, have a solid academic background, and are ready to contribute to research of the highest international standard. At Aarhus BSS, you will become part of an active and international research environment within the fields of business and social sciences. The Aarhus BSS Graduate School currently has more than 200 PhD students and admits more than 60 new candidates from around the world each year. Graduates of our PhD programmes pursue rewarding academic careers at the national and international levels, and many also move into public- and private-sector positions outside academia. The PhD programmes As a PhD student, you will be enrolled in one of our six PhD programmes and affiliated with a recognised research environment at one of the departments within Aarhus BSS. We offer PhD scholarships within the following programmes: Management Economics and Business Economics Law Political Science Psychology and Behavioural Sciences Business Development and Technology You can read more about the six PhD programmes here . Who are we looking for? We are seeking candidates who: have solid academic qualifications can formulate a clear, original, and relevant research proposal possess keen analytical skills and the motivation to complete a demanding PhD programme are interested in engaging in an international research environment What do we offer? Aarhus BSS is part of Aarhus University, an internationally recognised research university with well-established academic environments and close engagement with society and industry. As a PhD student, you will gain: access to renowned researchers and international networks an engaging and supportive research environment a pathway to a research career or a career in the private or public sector We are committed to creating an inclusive environment and recognize diversity as a key asset. We encourage all qualified candidates to apply. Assessment Criteria Applications are assessed based on an overall evaluation of the applicant’s qualifications. Particular emphasis is placed on: the quality, originality, and relevance of the research proposal academic performance in both bachelor’s and master’s degree studies evidence of a demonstrated ability to produce substantial written work, such as a master’s thesis, during studies or in other contexts The final decision regarding admission is made by the faculty management based on an assessment of both the quality of the proposed project and the applicant’s ability to complete it within the prescribed timeframe. Applicants are encouraged to include documentation of their class ranking (e.g. ranking or percentile), as this provides additional context for the assessment. However, this is not a requirement. Framework for the PhD Programme The PhD programme is conducted in accordance with the current Danish Ministerial Order on the PhD Programme and the rules and guidelines for PhD students at Aarhus BSS, both of which can be found here . It is not essential that your educational background matches the PhD programme exactly. The most important consideration is that your project is academically relevant and can be anchored within the research areas of the PhD programme. How to Apply If you wish to apply for a PhD position in Psychology and Behavioural Sciences, use the apply-button in this call. If you instead wish to apply for a PhD position in one of the other PhD programmes, please follow the link to the relevant PhD programme below. Management Economics and Business Economics Law Political Science Business Development and Technology You can read more about the application requirements in our Application Guide and find answers to frequently asked questions in our FAQ . If you need assistance with uploading your application or have questions regarding the recruitment process, please contact bss.hr@au.dk . Please indicate which programme you wish to apply for. Terms of Employment If admitted to the 3-year PhD programme, you will also be offered employment in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities (in Danish) and the collective agreement for academics employed by the Danish state (in Danish). The job description and qualification requirements are described in further detail in the Ministerial Order on the Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. It is also possible to be enrolled through the 4+4 PhD scheme. To qualify, applicants must have commenced a relevant master’s degree programme and completed 60 ECTS credits based on a relevant qualifying bachelor’s degree. You can read more about the structure of the PhD programme here . Salary and employment terms are governed by the collective agreement for academics employed by the Danish state . You will be appointed as a PhD fellow at base pay level 4–8, depending on your educational background and qualifications.The anticipated starting date is 1 February 2027. Place of Work Your place of work will depend on the department with which you are affiliated: Department of Management: Universitetsbyen 61–63, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark Department of Economics and Business Economics: Universitetsbyen 51, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark Department of Law: Bartholins Allé 16, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark Department of Political Science: Bartholins Allé 7, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences: Bartholins Allé 11, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark Department of Business Development and Technology: Birk Centerpark 15, 7400 Herning, Denmark Aarhus University Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Questions about the position\n                            ? Randi Groslier Bjælde PhD Consultant, Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4587164939 rgb@au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4593509350 bss.hr@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Monday  7 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks 2 days This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .pure.au.dk 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __Secure-typo3nonce_ouB7_tePaslDY7zpIHG6wg aias.au.dk Session __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .linkedin.com 29 minutes 59 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. __cf_bm Cloudflare Inc. .twitter.com 29 minutes 58 seconds This cookie is used to distinguish between humans and bots. This is beneficial for the website, in order to make valid reports on the use of their website. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. cf_clearance Cloudflare, Inc. .podbean.com 1 year This cookie is used by the CloudFlare service to identify trusted web traffic and override any security restrictions based on the visitor's IP address. It is essential for supporting a website's security features and in providing protection against malicious visitors. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .docs.workzone.kmd.net Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. XSRF-TOKEN event.au.dk 1 hour 59 minutes This cookie is written to help with site security in preventing Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks. li_gc LinkedIn Corporation .linkedin.com 5 months 4 weeks Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes x-ms-gateway-slice Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com Session Identifies a gateway for load balancing. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. eddiprod.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. brwConsent .airtable.com 5 minutes This cookie is used to record the user's consent to the use of cookies on the website, ensuring compliance with the website's privacy policy by remembering the user's preferences and consent state regarding cookies. CFTOKEN Adobe Inc. mit.au.dk Session Cookie set by Adobe ColdFusion applications. Used in conjunction with CFID this cookie helps to uniquely identify a client device (browser) to enable the site to maintain user session variables. How those are used are specific to the site. CFTOKEN contains a random number to identify the client. OptanonAlertBoxClosed OneTrust LLC .pure.au.dk 1 year This cookie is set by websites using certain versions of the cookie law compliance solution from OneTrust. It is set after visitors have seen a cookie information notice and in some cases only when they actively close the notice down. It enables the website not to show the message more than once to a user. The cookie has a one year lifespan and contains no personal information. PHPSESSID PHP.net internationalstaff.app3.geckobooking.dk Session Cookie generated by applications based on the PHP language. This is a general purpose identifier used to maintain user session variables. It is normally a random generated number, how it is used can be specific to the site, but a good example is maintaining a logged-in status for a user between pages. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .ofn.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .www.linkedin.com Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ASPSESSIONIDSQQCSQRC webforms.au.dk Session This cookie name is generally associated with use as a general purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Microsoft ASP based technologies. The structure of the cookie name is a common root - ASPSESSIONID, followed by a series of unique letters. It is usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. __RequestVerificationToken Microsoft Corporation forms.cloud.microsoft Session This is an anti-forgery cookie set by web applications built using ASP.NET MVC technologies. It is designed to stop unauthorised posting of content to a website, known as Cross-Site Request Forgery. It holds no information about the user and is destroyed on closing the browser. ARRAffinitySameSite Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session When using Microsoft Azure as a hosting platform and enabling load balancing, this cookie ensures that  requests from one visitor browsing session are always handled by the same server in the cluster. __Secure-typo3nonce_5BBMWw-Vqa1kCJ-0Zd