at pages you have visited, whether your computer, tablet or smartphone has used the pages before, which website you came from, which browser and operating system you use and the like. In some cases, IP addresses are also collected, which are personally identifiable data. Therefore, you can also read our Privacy Policy , which tells how we at AU process personal information. If any of the third party services, we use, process data on behalf of AU, we will, if possible, enter into a Data Processing Agreement with them. The supplier is thus not allowed to use the data for their own purposes or to pass them on to others. Delete cookies It is also possible to delete or block cookies. See the guide: https://www.allaboutcookies.org/manage-cookies/clear-cookies-installed.html The website is owned and published by: Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 DK-8000 Aarhus C Tel. no: 87 15 00 00 Email: au@au.dk Cookies consent ID : Cookie report created by CookieScript"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/studentermedhjaelper-til-sociale-medier-og-videoproduktion-paa-au-herning": {
      "title": "Studentermedhjælper til sociale medier og videoproduktion på AU Herning",
      "description": "Studentermedhjælper til sociale medier og videoproduktion på AU Herning - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Business Development and Technology Studentermedhjælper til sociale medier og videoproduktion på AU Herning Deadline 13 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Oct Department of Business Development and Technology Birk Centerpark 15 7400 Herning Part-time position 7.5 hours per week ID: 166837 Apply Er du studerende, og vil du være med til at skabe indhold, der bliver set, delt og husket på sociale medier? Så er du måske vores nye kommunikationsmedhjælper på AU Herning. Vi søger dig, der elsker storytelling i visuelle formater og har en naturlig fornemmelse for, hvad der fungerer på sociale medier. Som en del af kommunikationsteamet i Herning kommer du til at arbejde med markedsføring af vores uddannelser og produktion af kreativt indhold til vores digitale kanaler. Opgaverne spænder fra korte videoklip og tekster til reels og optagelser fra events, hvor du fanger øjeblikke og historier, der engagerer vores målgrupper. Du får selvfølgelig en god oplæring og introduktion til opgaverne, så du gradvist bliver klædt på til rollen og med tiden kan sætte dit eget præg på indholdet. Naturligvis med tæt sparring undervejs. Herudover er det et plus, hvis du har lyst til at være ambassadør for AU Herning og deltage i arrangementer og events både i og uden for huset. Hvem er du? Du er sandsynligvis studerende på AU Herning, kommunikationsstuderende eller lignende, men din baggrund er ikke så afgørende. Det vigtigste er, at du er idérig og har lyst til at skabe kreativt indhold, der fortæller den gode historie og inspirerer målgrupperne. Du følger med i trends, spotter idéer i hverdagen og trives både foran og bag kameraet. Du tør også række ud til medstuderende, undervisere og andre for at gøre dine contentidéer til virkelighed. Dine arbejdsopgaver bliver bl.a. at: planlægge, producere og redigere indhold til forskellige målgrupper på Instagram, LinkedIn og Facebook deltage i arrangementer på AU Herning med henblik på at skabe indhold til website og sociale medier Vi forventer, at du: kan finde ud af det der med billeder, video, redigering, grafisk design osv. er nysgerrig, initiativrig og ansvarsfuld er studerende på en videregående uddannelse – gerne inden for kommunikation og/eller marketing ikke er bange for at lære nye ting og få feedback Det får du: erfaring som content creator på CV’et fleksible arbejdstider, der giver plads til dit studie kontorplads på AU Herning tæt på kommunikationsteamet (med mulighed for at arbejde hjemme efter aftale) engagerede, søde og dedikerede kollegaer på tværs af huset Hvor skal du arbejde? Arbejdspladsen er AU Herning, Birk Centerpark 15, 7400 Herning. Du er selv i høj grad med til at tilrettelægge din arbejdstid og præge dine arbejdsopgaver i samarbejde med vores kommunikationskonsulent Lene Weyergang, som du også refererer til. Ansættelsesvilkår og løn Du bliver ansat som timelønnet studentermedhjælper med løn og andre ansættelsesvilkår i overensstemmelse med organisationsaftalen mellem Finansministeriet og HK/Stat. Arbejdstiden er på gennemsnitligt 7,5 timer om ugen, og timerne er som udgangspunkt placeret mellem kl. 8 og 16 i Herning. Dine mødetider er fleksible, så dine timer kan f.eks. samles på én hel dag eller to halve. Og der er mulighed for ekstra fleksibilitet i eksamens- og ferieperioder. Ansøgningsfrist 13. september 2026 Send os din ansøgning og dit CV, hvor du fortæller lidt om dig selv via link ”Søg stillingen” nederst på siden. Har du spørgsmål? Du er meget velkommen til at skrive eller ringe til kommunikationskonsulent Lene Weyergang på tlf. 28 29 21 05 eller e-mail lenew@btech.au.dk, hvis du har spørgsmål til stillingen. Aarhus Universitet vil være en attraktiv og inspirerende arbejdsplads for alle og ønsker en kultur, hvor hver enkelt kan udfolde og udvikle sig. Vi ser ligestilling og diversitet som en styrke og opfordrer derfor alle interesserede til at ansøge. Din ansøgning skal sendes via Aarhus Universitets rekrutteringssystem, som du finder under stillingsopslaget på Aarhus Universitets hjemmeside Questions about the position\n                            ? Lene Weyergang Communications Consultant, Department of Business Development and Technology +4528292105 lenew@btech.au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4593509350 bss.hr@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Sunday 13 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by