      "title": "A two-year Postdoctoral position in the research project: Advancing Building in School: Science and technology in SHAPE (ABIS)",
      "description": "A two-year Postdoctoral position in the research project: Advancing Building in School: Science and technology in SHAPE (ABIS) - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU Danish website You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability Campus development History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact School of Culture and Society - History of Ideas, subject - Faculty: Arts A two-year Postdoctoral position in the research project: Advancing Building in School: Science and technology in SHAPE (ABIS) Deadline 29 Sep 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Feb School of Culture and Society - History of Ideas, subject Jens Chr. Skous Vej 7 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Feb 2027 - 31 Jan 2029 ID: 168133 Apply The research project Advancing Bildung in School: Science and Technology in SHAPE (ABIS) invites applications for a two-year postdoctoral position based in the Department of Philosophy and History of Ideas at Aarhus University. ABIS is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation and is a collaboration between four partner institutions, with the University of Southern Denmark (SDU) serving as the lead institution. ABIS is an empirically grounded research project that explores how humanities and social science subjects in schools (SHAPE subjects) can develop ways of knowing about science and technology that contribute to Bildung [dannelse]. The position is expected to begin from February 1 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The place of work will be Aarhus University, Jens Chr. Skous Vej 7, 8000 Aarhus C. Read more about the ABIS Project here: https://www.sdu.dk/da/nyheder/nnf_bevilling_dannelsesbegreb The position The position contributes to the theoretical and innovative work of the ABIS project, which develops the epistemological and didactical foundations for advancing Bildung through the integration of science and technology within SHAPE subjects To support this work, we are seeking a scholar with a solid background in fields such as Science Studies, Educational Research, Subject education, History of Ideas and Philosophy, or other relevant disciplines. The two-year postdoctoral position focuses on bridging research on scientific and technological literacy with Bildung traditions and conceptualisations, thereby building the foundations for didactical frameworks that integrate science and technology within SHAPE subjects focusing here mainly on History/historie, L1/dansk, and Social Science/samfundsfag. The research is expected to result in high-quality international publications, including both co-authored and single-authored works, that advance scholarship on the relationships between scientific literacy, technological literacy, and Bildung . Expected research outputs also include contributing to the organisation of academic conferences, as well as a range of outreach and knowledge dissemination activities, including the ABIS project teacher education program Department of Philosophy and History of Ideas at the School of Culture and Society at AU and the ABIS project are committed to cultivating a diverse and inclusive academic community. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, regardless of personal background, because we believe diverse perspectives and experiences improve research, support collaboration, and deepen our shared engagement with society. Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD degree in history of ideas, science studies, philosophy, educational research, subject education, or related areas relevant to the position or they must document equal qualifications. The selected candidate will be expected to: Document an international research profile Be well-versed in research on scientific and technological literacy, as well as in debates concerning the Nature of Science and the Nature of Technology, their educational implications, and their relationship to Bildung Have a well-developed understanding of the epistemological dimensions of both science and the humanities and their implications in didactical contexts Have an excellent command of English for international academic publishing and a good command of Danish, as the empirical basis and intervention activities of the ABIS project are closely connected to the Danish educational context from primary to upper-secondary levels and require engagement with Danish-language sources, participants, and stakeholders Be motivated to work closely with both junior and senior colleagues and thrive in a collaborative research environment devoted to generating innovative knowledge and practice on the integration of science and technology in Bildung in SHAPE subjects Have a genuine interest in engaging with and learning from stakeholders beyond academia, including teachers, policymakers and other professionals involved in education In addition, the applicant must supply: A concise statement of motivation for applying for the position, and a short outline of how the applicant would approach the proposed topic and tasks. Certificates/Diplomas for academic degrees. A maximum of two publications relevant for the application. Please attach one pdf-file for each publication. Only submitted publications will be assessed; a list of publications is not sufficient. As a result, applications without submitted publications will not be assessed. a CV (maximum three pages) Professional references or recommendations should not be included. Applicants who are selected for an interview may be asked to provide professional references. The application must be submitted in either English or Danish. For further information about the position and the project, please contact:  Professor Casper Andersen ideca@cas.au.dk For more information about the application and the employment procedure, please contact HR iks-hr-sag@au.dk The work environment The selected applicant will be based at the School of Culture and Society, Aarhus University, Department of Philosophy and History of Ideas, Jens Christian Skous vej 7, 8000 Aarhus C. The Department of employs about 25 tenured full and associate professors, plus post-doctoral researchers and a cohort of approximately 15 PhD students. Read more [link] The department will serve as the primary workplace, and regular presence is expected in order to support active participation in the research environment, including seminars, project meetings, and collaboration with colleagues. As the ABIS project is also anchored at the University of Southern Denmark, the selected applicant should also expect to participate regularly in project meetings, workshops, and other relevant activities with colleagues there. The selected candidate should expect a certain amount of travel due to the project’s cross-institutional nature. The School of Culture and Society The School of Culture and Society is a vibrant research community dedicated to understanding the cultural and social conditions that shape human life. Our work examines how people interact with their environments, from prehistory to the present, and across both local contexts and global dynamics. Through cross-sector and cross-disciplinary partnerships, we aim to drive research innovation and contribute to address the major questions facing society. In both research and education, we are committed to bringing the humanities into active dialogue with partners beyond the university. The School is committed to: Fostering an international environment characterized by strong academic and interdisciplinary collaboration. Embracing an innovative and experimental approach to research, teaching, and communication. Cultivating a school that both generates knowledge and educates students for the present and future. Advancing a broad engagement with digital humanities. Upholding a strong commitment to both local and global societal challenges. Creating an inclusive, diverse, and sustainable workplace and organization. Read more about the school here School of Culture and Society - Aarhus University International applicants International applicants are encouraged to check Family and work-life balance in Denmark (au.dk) and Attractive working conditions (au.dk) for further information about the benefits of working at Aarhus University and in Denmark, including healthcare, paid holidays and, if relevant, maternity/paternity leave, childcare and schooling. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including a Relocation and onboarding services for international AU staff and career counselling for expat partners. For information about taxation, see Taxation aspects of international researchers’ employment by AU . Qualification requirements Applicants should hold a PhD or equivalent academic qualifications. Formalities Faculty of Arts refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities (the Appointment Order) . Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Further information on the application and supplementary materials may be found in Application Guidelines . The application must outline the applicant's motivation for applying for the position, attaching a curriculum vitae, a complete list of published works, copies of degree certificates and examples of academic production ( mandatory, but no more than two examples ). Please upload this material electronically along with your application. Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here: https://talent.au.dk/junior-researcher-development-programme/ If nothing else is noted, applications must be submitted in English. Application deadline is at 11.59 pm Danish time (same as Central European Time) on the deadline day. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Shortlists may be prepared with the candidates that have been selected for a detailed academic assessment. A committee set up by the head of school is responsible for selecting the most qualified candidates. See this link for further information about shortlisting at the Faculty of Arts: shortlisting Terms of employment Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Finance and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Salary and terms of employment are governed by the Cirkulære om overenskomst for akademikere i staten (in Danish). You will be employed as post doctoral fellow at base pay level 4–8 with additional supplements in accordance with the Cirkulære om protokollat om visse ansættelsesvilkår for videnskabeligt personale ved universiteter (in Danish). The job content and qualification requirements are described in further detail in the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of  Academic Staff at Universities . About Arts The Faculty of Arts is one of Northern Europe’s most significant faculties for research and higher education in the humanities, theology and education. Within this broad academic scope, the faculty comprises approximately 700 researchers, 200 PhD students, 9,000 Bachelor’s and Master’s degree students, and 1,500 further and continuing education students. We believe that the best ideas arise when different perspectives meet – and that research, teaching and innovation are best developed in dialogue with the surrounding society. You can find more information here: Faculty of Arts | Aarhus University The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website . Questions about the position\n                            ? Casper Andersen Professor, Research Programm Director, School of Culture and Society - History of Ideas, subject +4526391325 ideca@cas.au.dk Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Arts Administrative Centre - Arts HR +4593521049 emply.ar.hr@au.dk Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday 29 Sep 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: au@au.dk Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48 English Danish Cookies improve user experience When you click 'Accept all' cookies, Aarhus University can give you the best user experience. Cookies store information about how a user interacts with a website. All your data is anonymised and cannot be used to identify you. You can always change your consent again under ‘Cookies' in the website footer. The university uses its own cookies and cookies set by our partners. Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified Save & Close Accept all Decline all Read more about cookies Hide details List of cookies Cookie Policy Strictly necessary Statistic Targeting Functionality Unclassified These cookies make it possible to use basic website functionality, e.g. navigation etc. The website does not work without these cookies. Cookie report Name Provider / Domain Expires Description be_typo_user TYPO3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is set by our CMS provider; TYPO3 and is used to identify a backend session when a Backend User is logged in to TYPO3 Backend or Frontend. fe_typo_user Typo3 Association .au.dk 30 minutes This cookie is associated with the Typo3 web content management system. It is generally used as a user session identifier to enable user preferences to be stored, but in many cases it may not actually be needed as it can be set by default by the platform, though this can be prevented by site administrators. In most cases it is set to be destroyed at the end of a browser session. It contains a random identifier rather than any specific user data. ASP.NET_SessionId Microsoft Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written with Miscrosoft .NET based technologies. Usually used to maintain an anonymised user session by the server. JSESSIONID Oracle Corporation .au.dk Session General purpose platform session cookie, used by sites written in JSP. Usually used to maintain an anonymous user session by the server. ARRAffinity Microsoft Corporation .mitstudie.au.dk Session This cookie is set by websites run on the Windows Azure cloud platform. It is used for load balancing to make sure the visitor page requests are routed to the same server in any browsing session. esctx Microsoft Corporation .login.microsoftonline.com Session This cookie is used by Microsoft to securely verify your login information fpc Microsoft Corporation login.microsoftonline.com 4 weeks